569
00:29:06,910 --> 00:29:13,430
Yes, simple and useful English that you can use in meetings, presentations, and daily business

570
00:29:13,430 --> 00:29:14,630
communication.

571
00:29:14,630 --> 00:29:18,830
If you enjoy learning with us, please like this video and subscribe to our channel.

572
00:29:18,830 --> 00:29:21,670
It really helps us create more lessons for you.

573
00:29:21,670 --> 00:29:23,070
Thank you so much!

574
00:29:23,070 --> 00:29:26,470
Today, we are going to talk about an important business topic.

575
00:29:26,470 --> 00:29:27,470
That's right.

576
00:29:27,470 --> 00:29:32,750
Today, we will discuss how to explain a project you worked on in English.

577
00:29:32,750 --> 00:29:35,390
This is a very useful skill in business.

578
00:29:35,390 --> 00:29:39,430
Many jobs require you to talk about projects, tasks, and results.

579
00:29:39,430 --> 00:29:45,470
For example, in interviews, meetings, or reports, you may need to describe your work.

580
00:29:45,470 --> 00:29:49,790
So today, we will practice simple and professional ways to explain a project.

581
00:29:49,790 --> 00:29:54,070
We will use easy English so you can understand and practice.

582
00:29:54,070 --> 00:29:55,070
Let's get started.

583
00:29:55,070 --> 00:29:56,750
Daniel, how are you today?

584
00:29:56,750 --> 00:29:58,070
I'm doing well, thank you.

585
00:29:58,070 --> 00:30:00,710
I feel a little busy, but it's a good kind of busy.

586
00:30:00,710 --> 00:30:02,270
That sounds productive.

587
00:30:02,270 --> 00:30:06,030
Being busy usually means we are working on important tasks.

588
00:30:06,030 --> 00:30:08,870
Yes, I was working on a small project this morning.

589
00:30:08,870 --> 00:30:10,550
Oh, that's interesting.

590
00:30:10,550 --> 00:30:12,110
What kind of project was it?

591
00:30:12,110 --> 00:30:13,530
It was a marketing project.

592
00:30:13,530 --> 00:30:16,650
We were creating ideas for a new advertisement campaign.

593
00:30:16,650 --> 00:30:18,510
That sounds like important work.

594
00:30:18,510 --> 00:30:19,510
It is.

595
00:30:19,510 --> 00:30:22,710
Marketing helps businesses reach customers and communicate their value.

596
00:30:22,710 --> 00:30:26,430
So today, maybe you can explain that project to us.

597
00:30:26,430 --> 00:30:28,670
Sure, I can explain it in simple English.

598
00:30:28,670 --> 00:30:31,430
That would be great practice for our viewers.

599
00:30:31,430 --> 00:30:32,870
Okay, let's begin.

600
00:30:32,870 --> 00:30:35,630
First, tell us the basic information.

601
00:30:35,630 --> 00:30:37,310
What was the project about?

602
00:30:37,310 --> 00:30:40,230
The project was about creating an advertisement campaign

603
00:30:40,230 --> 00:30:41,430
for a new product.

604
00:30:41,430 --> 00:30:42,750
What was the product?

605
00:30:42,750 --> 00:30:44,150
It was a mobile application

606
00:30:44,150 --> 00:30:46,670
that helps people organize their daily tasks.

607
00:30:46,670 --> 00:30:47,950
That sounds useful.

608
00:30:47,950 --> 00:30:50,070
Yes, the idea was to show customers

609
00:30:50,070 --> 00:30:53,310
how the application can save time and improve productivity.

610
00:30:53,310 --> 00:30:56,110
So your goal was to promote the product

611
00:30:56,110 --> 00:30:58,190
and explain its benefits.

612
00:30:58,190 --> 00:30:59,030
Exactly.

613
00:30:59,030 --> 00:31:01,750
Marketing is about communication and value.

614
00:31:01,750 --> 00:31:02,910
That makes sense.

615
00:31:02,910 --> 00:31:05,110
Businesses need to explain why customers

616
00:31:05,110 --> 00:31:06,470
should use their products.

617
00:31:06,470 --> 00:31:09,070
Let's talk about your role in the project.

618
00:31:09,070 --> 00:31:10,270
What did you do?

619
00:31:10,270 --> 00:31:13,150
My role was to create ideas for the advertisement.

620
00:31:13,150 --> 00:31:15,390
Can you explain that in more detail?

621
00:31:15,390 --> 00:31:16,070
Sure.

622
00:31:16,070 --> 00:31:17,870
I researched customer preferences

623
00:31:17,870 --> 00:31:19,710
and suggested marketing messages.

624
00:31:19,710 --> 00:31:22,230
What does marketing message mean?

625
00:31:22,230 --> 00:31:24,390
A marketing message is the main idea

626
00:31:24,390 --> 00:31:26,410
you want customers to understand.

627
00:31:26,410 --> 00:31:29,370
For example, why the product is useful.

628
00:31:29,370 --> 00:31:30,210
Exactly.

629
00:31:30,210 --> 00:31:32,810
In our project, the message was that the application

630
00:31:32,810 --> 00:31:34,450
helps people save time.

631
00:31:34,450 --> 00:31:36,290
That sounds clear and simple.

632
00:31:36,290 --> 00:31:39,090
Yes, clear messages are important in marketing.

633
00:31:39,090 --> 00:31:41,530
Did you work alone or with a team?

634
00:31:41,530 --> 00:31:42,770
I worked with a team.

635
00:31:42,770 --> 00:31:45,410
Teamwork is very important in business projects.

636
00:31:45,410 --> 00:31:46,250
I agree.

637
00:31:46,250 --> 00:31:48,610
Different people bring different ideas.

638
00:31:48,610 --> 00:31:49,610
Exactly.

639
00:31:49,610 --> 00:31:51,850
Our team included designers, writers,

640
00:31:51,850 --> 00:31:53,290
and marketing specialists.

641
00:31:53,290 --> 00:31:55,170
What did the designers do?

642
00:31:55,170 --> 00:31:57,970
The designers created visuals for the advertisement.

643
00:31:57,970 --> 00:32:01,730
Visuals mean images and design elements, right?

644
00:32:01,730 --> 00:32:05,370
Yes, visuals help attract attention and communicate ideas.

645
00:32:05,370 --> 00:32:07,250
What did the writers do?

646
00:32:07,250 --> 00:32:10,010
The writers created text for the advertisement.

647
00:32:10,010 --> 00:32:12,490
Like slogans and descriptions.

648
00:32:12,490 --> 00:32:13,490
Exactly.

649
00:32:13,490 --> 00:32:16,530
A slogan is a short phrase that communicates a message.

650
00:32:16,530 --> 00:32:19,650
For example, save time, live better.

651
00:32:19,650 --> 00:32:20,850
That is a good example.

652
00:32:20,850 --> 00:32:23,650
Short and memorable slogans work well in marketing.

653
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:25,610
So your team worked together

654
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,650
on different parts of the project?

655
00:32:27,650 --> 00:32:30,530
Yes, teamwork helped us create a better result.

656
00:32:30,530 --> 00:32:31,850
That is a good point.

657
00:32:31,850 --> 00:32:34,290
Collaboration improves quality.

658
00:32:34,290 --> 00:32:35,170
Absolutely.

659
00:32:35,170 --> 00:32:37,490
No one can do anything alone in business.

660
00:32:37,490 --> 00:32:39,370
Let's talk about the process.

661
00:32:39,370 --> 00:32:41,250
How did you start the project?

662
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:43,690
First, we researched the target audience.

663
00:32:43,690 --> 00:32:45,810
What is target audience?

664
00:32:45,810 --> 00:32:47,850
The target audience is the group of people

665
00:32:47,850 --> 00:32:49,130
you want to reach.

666
00:32:49,130 --> 00:32:52,490
For example, customers who might use the product.

667
00:32:52,490 --> 00:32:56,570
Exactly. In our project, the target audience was busy professionals.

668
00:32:56,570 --> 00:32:58,450
Why busy professionals?

669
00:32:58,450 --> 00:33:01,330
Because the application helps people manage their time.

670
00:33:01,330 --> 00:33:02,370
That makes sense.

671
00:33:02,370 --> 00:33:05,770
Busy professionals often need productivity tools.

672
00:33:05,770 --> 00:33:08,130
Yes, so we focused our marketing messages

673
00:33:08,130 --> 00:33:10,050
on time management benefits.

674
00:33:10,050 --> 00:33:12,410
What did you do after research?

675
00:33:12,410 --> 00:33:15,290
After research, we planned the marketing strategy.

676
00:33:15,290 --> 00:33:19,330
Strategy means the plan you follow to achieve your goal.

677
00:33:19,330 --> 00:33:20,330
Exactly.

678
00:33:20,330 --> 00:33:23,370
Our strategy was to highlight the product's advantages.

679
00:33:23,370 --> 00:33:25,690
What advantages did you emphasize?

680
00:33:25,690 --> 00:33:28,730
We emphasized ease of use and time-saving features.

681
00:33:28,730 --> 00:33:31,290
That sounds like a strong marketing approach.

682
00:33:31,290 --> 00:33:34,650
Yes, customers want solutions that make life easier.

683
00:33:34,650 --> 00:33:36,690
How long did the project take?

684
00:33:36,690 --> 00:33:38,210
It took about three weeks.

685
00:33:38,210 --> 00:33:41,010
That is a reasonable time for a marketing project.

686
00:33:41,010 --> 00:33:44,730
Yes, we needed time to research, plan, and create content.

687
00:33:44,730 --> 00:33:46,610
Did you face any challenges?

688
00:33:46,610 --> 00:33:48,930
Yes, every project has challenges.

689
00:33:48,930 --> 00:33:50,770
What challenges did you face?

690
00:33:50,770 --> 00:33:53,570
One challenge was finding the right marketing message.

691
00:33:53,570 --> 00:33:55,090
Why was that difficult?

692
00:33:55,090 --> 00:33:57,930
Because different customers value different benefits.

693
00:33:57,930 --> 00:34:01,170
For example, some customers care about price

694
00:34:01,170 --> 00:34:03,450
and others care about features.

695
00:34:03,450 --> 00:34:04,290
Exactly.

696
00:34:04,290 --> 00:34:07,090
We needed a message that appealed to many customers.

697
00:34:07,090 --> 00:34:09,010
How did you solve that problem?

698
00:34:09,010 --> 00:34:12,290
We discussed ideas as a team and tested different messages.

699
00:34:12,290 --> 00:34:14,690
Testing ideas is a good strategy.

700
00:34:14,690 --> 00:34:17,190
Yes. Feedback helps improve results.

701
00:34:17,190 --> 00:34:18,690
What is feedback?

702
00:34:18,690 --> 00:34:22,190
Feedback is information about performance or quality.

703
00:34:22,190 --> 00:34:25,690
For example, comments from colleagues or customers.

704
00:34:25,690 --> 00:34:28,690
Exactly. Feedback helps you learn and improve.

705
00:34:28,690 --> 00:34:31,190
Did you receive feedback on your project?

706
00:34:31,190 --> 00:34:33,690
Yes. We received feedback from our manager.

707
00:34:33,690 --> 00:34:35,190
Was the feedback positive?

708
00:34:35,190 --> 00:34:37,690
It was both positive and constructive.

709
00:34:37,690 --> 00:34:40,190
What does constructive feedback mean?

710
00:34:40,190 --> 00:34:43,690
Constructive feedback helps improvement in a helpful way.

711
00:34:43,690 --> 00:34:44,970
That sounds useful.

712
00:34:44,970 --> 00:34:48,010
Yes, feedback is important for professional growth.

713
00:34:48,010 --> 00:34:49,850
Let's talk about results.

714
00:34:49,850 --> 00:34:52,010
What was the outcome of the project?

715
00:34:52,010 --> 00:34:53,530
The outcome was positive.

716
00:34:53,530 --> 00:34:56,010
The advertisement campaign attracted attention.

717
00:34:56,010 --> 00:34:57,530
That sounds successful.

718
00:34:57,530 --> 00:35:00,570
Yes, we received good responses from potential customers.

719
00:35:00,570 --> 00:35:02,170
Did sales increase?

720
00:35:02,170 --> 00:35:05,450
It was a marketing project, so we focused on awareness.

721
00:35:05,450 --> 00:35:08,970
Awareness means customers knowing about the product.

722
00:35:08,970 --> 00:35:12,170
Exactly, awareness is the first step in marketing.

723
00:35:12,170 --> 00:35:13,210
That makes sense.

724
00:35:13,210 --> 00:35:16,650
Customers need to know about a product before buying it.

725
00:35:16,650 --> 00:35:19,370
Yes, marketing helps communicate value.

726
00:35:19,370 --> 00:35:22,330
Let's talk about what you learned from the project.

727
00:35:22,330 --> 00:35:25,530
I learned many things about teamwork and communication.

728
00:35:25,530 --> 00:35:27,450
That is important in business.

729
00:35:27,450 --> 00:35:30,570
Yes, communication helps teams work effectively.

730
00:35:30,570 --> 00:35:32,010
What else did you learn?

731
00:35:32,010 --> 00:35:34,490
I learned how to analyze customer needs.

732
00:35:34,490 --> 00:35:36,250
That is a valuable skill.

733
00:35:36,250 --> 00:35:40,250
Businesses must understand customer needs to create good solutions.

734
00:35:40,250 --> 00:35:43,050
Do you feel the project improved your skills?

735
00:35:43,050 --> 00:35:46,410
Yes, it helped me improve marketing and problem-solving skills.

736
00:35:46,410 --> 00:35:48,490
That sounds like professional growth.

737
00:35:48,490 --> 00:35:51,930
Exactly. Every project is an opportunity to learn.

738
00:35:51,930 --> 00:35:55,930
Now, let's practice explaining the project in simple English.

739
00:35:55,930 --> 00:35:58,650
Good idea. I will give a short explanation.

740
00:35:58,650 --> 00:35:59,530
Go ahead.

741
00:35:59,530 --> 00:36:02,890
Okay. The project was about marketing a mobile application.

742
00:36:03,450 --> 00:36:06,490
My role was to create ideas for the advertisement.

743
00:36:06,490 --> 00:36:10,250
I worked with a team to research customers and plan marketing messages.

744
00:36:10,250 --> 00:36:13,370
We focused on time-saving benefits and ease of use.

745
00:36:13,370 --> 00:36:16,730
The project took three weeks and received positive feedback.

746
00:36:16,730 --> 00:36:18,970
I learned about teamwork and communication.

747
00:36:18,970 --> 00:36:22,490
That was a great explanation, clear and professional.

748
00:36:22,490 --> 00:36:25,850
Thank you. Simple language works well in business communication.

749
00:36:25,850 --> 00:36:28,650
Now let's summarize what we discussed today.

750
00:36:28,650 --> 00:36:31,770
We talked about how to explain a project in English.

751
00:36:31,770 --> 00:36:36,570
We discussed project goals, roles, challenges, and results.

752
00:36:36,570 --> 00:36:39,290
And we used simple business English phrases.

753
00:36:39,290 --> 00:36:42,810
Explaining projects is an important professional skill.

754
00:36:42,810 --> 00:36:46,090
Yes, it helps communication in interviews and meetings.

755
00:36:46,090 --> 00:36:48,410
Now it's your turn to practice.

756
00:36:48,410 --> 00:36:49,930
Here is a question for you.

757
00:36:49,930 --> 00:36:52,730
Can you explain a project you worked on?

758
00:36:52,730 --> 00:36:55,370
Try to describe the project in simple English.

759
00:36:55,370 --> 00:36:58,970
You can mention the goal, your role, and the results.

760
00:36:58,970 --> 00:37:00,730
Any practice is good practice.

761
00:37:00,730 --> 00:37:02,490
Thank you for joining us today.

762
00:37:02,490 --> 00:37:05,930
We hope this conversation helps you improve your business English.

763
00:37:05,930 --> 00:37:08,010
Keep practicing and learning.

764
00:37:08,010 --> 00:37:10,250
Business English is a valuable skill.

765
00:37:10,250 --> 00:37:11,450
Have a great day.

766
00:37:11,450 --> 00:37:13,130
